          "children": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Historical Context",
                  "textSize": "heading-four"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Latino USA",
                  "italic": true
                },
                {
                  "text": " is an award-winning radio program that explores news, culture, and issues affecting Latino communities in the United States. Established in 1993 by KUT Radio and the Center for Mexican American Studies at the University of Texas at Austin, the program was created to address the lack of Latino representation in nationally distributed public radio. Hosted by Maria Hinojosa, "
                },
                {
                  "text": "Latino USA",
                  "italic": true
                },
                {
                  "text": " aims to promote cross-cultural understanding by highlighting the diverse experiences and perspectives of Latino communities. Production transitioned to the Futuro Media Group in 2010."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": ""
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Project Description",
                  "textSize": "heading-four"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "In order to visually represent the"
                },
                {
                  "type": "link",
                  "url": "https://txarchives.org/utlac/finding_aids/00344.xml",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": " LLILAS Benson's Latino USA Radio Collection"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": ", we are using AVAnnotate to highlight areas of episodes focusing on immigration, cultural traditions of immigrants in the United States, and international relations. We focused on ten episodes individually linked below that heavily feature talk of immigration and immigrant cultural traditions. Each episode has been annotated through both subject and geographic tags that appear under each relevant time stamp. All our tags were selected from authorized"
                },
                {
                  "type": "link",
                  "url": "https://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects.html",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": " Library of Congress Subject Headings (LCSH)"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": ""
                },
                {
                  "type": "link",
                  "url": "https://www.arcgis.com/apps/mapviewer/index.html?webmap=ce94f8cd3f6049ebab968df5fa950809&center=-78.671872%2C28.648242&scale=147914381.897889",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": ""
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": ""
                },
                {
                  "type": "link",
                  "url": "https://www.arcgis.com/apps/mapviewer/index.html?webmap=ce94f8cd3f6049ebab968df5fa950809&center=-78.671872%2C28.648242&scale=147914381.897889",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "Interactive ArcGIS Map",
                      "textSize": "heading-four",
                      "underline": true
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "We have also integrated a map (hyperlinked above) identifying specific geographic regions mentioned throughout the episodes to understand how these places are represented and shaped by immigration discourses. This provides users with the opportunity to more easily navigate episodes based on geographic relevance while identifying broader patterns and trends in conversations about immigration."
                }
              ]
            },
